.TH WAVE-LINKQUERY 1 "" "MacWave" "MacWave Manual"

.SH NAME
wave-linkquery \- Show which version the versionless shortcut points at, as name => version. With no package (or with --all) it lists every installed package, two columns when the terminal is wide enough.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wave linkquery [<package> | \-\-all] [\-\-raw]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show which version the versionless shortcut points at, as name =>
version. With no package (or with --all) it lists every installed
package, two columns when the terminal is wide enough.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-all, \-a
Apply to every installed package (the default when no package is given)
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Plain output for scripts: one name@version per line, no emoji, no
columns

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
wave linkquery jq
wave linkquery --all
wave linkquery --raw
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
wave(1)
